            question: 'Explain the concept of mutual interdependence in oligopoly markets.',
            answer: 'Mutual interdependence:\n\nDefinition:\n- Each firm\'s profit depends not only on its own actions but also on rivals\' responses\n- Must anticipate competitors\' reactions when making decisions\n\nImplications:\n\n1. Price decisions:\n   - Cannot ignore rivals when changing prices\n   - Price cut may trigger price war\n   - Price increase may lose market share if rivals don\'t follow\n\n2. Output decisions:\n   - Increasing output affects market price\n   - Rivals may respond by adjusting their output\n\n3. Strategic behavior:\n   - Game theory applies\n   - Must consider multiple scenarios\n   - Uncertainty about rivals\' actions\n\n4. Collusion incentive:\n   - Firms may cooperate to avoid destructive competition\n   - Maximize joint profits\n   - But unstable due to cheating incentive\n\nContrast with perfect competition (no interdependence) and monopoly (no rivals).',
