            question: 'Explain tacit collusion and how it differs from explicit collusion.',
            answer: 'Tacit collusion:\n\nDefinition: Informal coordination without explicit agreement\n\nMechanisms:\n\n1. Price leadership:\n   - Dominant firm sets price\n   - Smaller firms follow\n   - No formal agreement needed\n   - Example: Barometric price leadership\n\n2. Parallel behavior:\n   - Firms independently reach similar decisions\n   - Observe and match rivals\' actions\n   - Focal points (e.g., round numbers)\n\n3. Trade associations:\n   - Information sharing\n   - Industry norms and standards\n   - Indirect coordination\n\nDifferences from explicit collusion:\n\nExplicit (cartel):\n- Formal agreement\n- Direct communication\n- Specific quotas and prices\n- Clearly illegal\n- More stable but risky\n\nTacit:\n- No formal agreement\n- Inferred coordination\n- General patterns\n- Legal gray area\n- Less stable but safer\n\nAdvantages of tacit collusion:\n- Avoids legal liability\n- More flexible\n- Easier to implement\n\nDisadvantages:\n- Less certain\n- Misunderstandings possible\n- Weaker compliance',
