            question: 'Compare and contrast the efficiency outcomes of oligopoly with other market structures.',
            answer: 'Allocative efficiency:\n- Perfect competition: P = MC ✓\n- Monopoly: P > MC ✗ (worst)\n- Oligopoly: P > MC ✗ (between competition and monopoly)\n- Depends on collusion level\n\nProductive efficiency:\n- Perfect competition: P = minimum AC ✓ (long run)\n- Monopoly: P ≠ minimum AC ✗\n- Oligopoly: May or may not produce at minimum AC\n- Often some excess capacity\n\nX-efficiency:\n- Perfect competition: High competitive pressure ✓\n- Monopoly: Low pressure, organizational slack ✗\n- Oligopoly: Moderate pressure from rivals\n- Less slack than monopoly, more than perfect competition\n\nDynamic efficiency:\n- Perfect competition: Low (no supernormal profits for R&D)\n- Monopoly: Potentially high (profits fund innovation) but weak incentive\n- Oligopoly: Often highest\n  * Supernormal profits available for R&D\n  * Strong competitive pressure drives innovation\n  * Examples: Tech industry, pharmaceuticals\n\nConclusion:\nOligopoly shows mixed efficiency:\n- Static inefficiency (allocative, productive)\n- Potential dynamic efficiency advantages\n- Outcome depends on degree of competition vs. collusion',
