            question: 'Explain how mergers and acquisitions (M&A) can be used as a competitive strategy in oligopolistic markets.',
            answer: 'M&A as competitive strategy:\n\nTypes:\n1. Horizontal integration - merge with competitor\n2. Vertical integration - merge with supplier or distributor\n3. Conglomerate - merge with unrelated business\n\nMotives in oligopoly:\n\n1. Increase market power:\n   - Reduce competition\n   - Gain pricing power\n   - Increase concentration ratio\n\n2. Economies of scale:\n   - Spread fixed costs over larger output\n   - Bulk purchasing discounts\n   - Rationalize operations\n\n3. Reduce rivalry:\n   - Eliminate competitor\n   - Less uncertainty from interdependence\n   - Easier to coordinate (fewer firms)\n\n4. Access to resources:\n   - Technology, patents, expertise\n   - Distribution networks\n   - Customer base\n\n5. Diversification:\n   - Spread risk across markets\n   - Counter seasonal variations\n   - Enter new markets quickly\n\nRegulatory concerns:\n- Competition authorities scrutinize mergers\n- May block if reduces competition substantially\n- Efficiency gains must outweigh competitive harm\n\nExamples: Tech giants acquiring startups, airline mergers, pharmaceutical consolidation',
